1
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:26,840
Aiming for the setting
sun over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too,

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,260
right onto the head of the
carpenter who was saving his money.

4
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,
Katsushika, there's no helping it.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,560
Even a yawn changes nothing;
the streets are strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:16,800
From the pointed-hat water jug,
the sunset drops down in its natural glow.

8
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it.

9
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happy again, they say.

10
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after I lost it.

11
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,880
Because I'm such a fool.

12
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:41,440
Outrageous Aerial Police Squad!

13
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,600
Hey, bro...

14
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,580
Ob-buh...

15
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,240
Yeah, yeah~

16
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:53,980
Y-you...

17
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,740
Wh-whoa, whoa, whoa!

18
00:01:58,060 --> 00:01:59,580
An ATM

19
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,200
Cash is humming away in there, isn't it?

20
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,420
Just a little, that's all. Give me some.

21
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,600
H-hey? Hey?

22
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:10,580
What?

23
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,080
You don't have to run away, you know.

24
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:14,320
Run away?

25
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,420
Dragon

26
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,220
It's shown up again

27
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:41,000
ATM robbery.

28
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,820
The one using that airplane.

29
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,060
That's already the fifth case.

30
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,300
It's other people's money anyway.

31
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,920
It's none of my business.

32
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:50,080
But it is your business.

33
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,540
Good morning, Chief.

34
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,900
Morning.

35
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,200
What do you mean, Chief?

36
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,140
Saying it concerns you, senpai?

37
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:01,720
The truth is, to solve this case,

38
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,940
an air police unit is going to be formed.

39
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,320
Air police unit?

40
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:08,600
So, the Air Police.

41
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,800
Air Police?

42
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,620
They've had those in America
and other places for a long time.

43
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,740
They use helicopters
in place of patrol cars.

44
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:23,120
That's right. You've been recommended to lead that air police unit,
you know.

45
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:30,980
Here's your recommendation letter. Isn't
it great? Suddenly being exiled like this!

46
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:38,820
Me, handpicked? So my brilliance has
finally reached the top of the police force.

47
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:41,520
I can only think it was a bad choice.

48
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,620
Who recommended you, senpai?

49
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:47,060
They say you'll be the technical
advisor for the air police unit.

50
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,120
I don't know the details myself.

51
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:52,680
This place somehow looks familiar.

52
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,880
This is the map to the air
police unit's headquarters.

53
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:57,840
Make sure you do a good job.

54
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,500
Chief, are you worried about me?

55
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,980
No, I just don't want you
coming back here ever again.

56
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:06,740
Yeah, I figured as much.

57
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:11,100
Anyway, what's with this map?

58
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:13,760
There's a mark on the bridge here.

59
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:16,860
The air police unit is really out here?

60
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,740
I've got a bad feeling about this.

61
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:23,520
W-what?

62
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:26,920
This is the headquarters?

63
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,020
The greatest genius of the Renaissance era,

64
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:34,080
Leonardo Dappinchi,

65
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,600
was invited by the Borgia family of Italy

66
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:39,680
and is said to have created
numerous works of art and inventions.

67
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,440
This voice... could it be?

68
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:45,660
Though none of them were
ever put into practical use,

69
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,320
there were also many
blueprints for airplanes.

70
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,140
Let's bring them back to
life in the modern day!

71
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:55,380
Ciao, long time no see, Gorilla-kun!

72
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:58,680
I knew it was you, Professor Esaki.

73
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:03,060
So the technical advisor who
recommended me as captain was...

74
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:04,420
Indeed, it was me.

75
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:06,580
I thought as much.

76
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:10,660
Hey, haven't the other members arrived yet?

77
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:12,980
Aren't they all here already?

78
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,880
So I was right, then.

79
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:19,800
The Japanese Air Police Unit begins with just the two of us,
you and me.

80
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,840
I don't want to be alone with you, Frog.

81
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,420
Wait, Gorilla-kun.

82
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,300
For now, it's just the two of us.

83
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:33,500
If we produce results,
the Air Police Unit will keep growing.

84
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:37,484
It'll grow to 10, 20, even 100 members,

85
00:05:37,534 --> 00:05:41,140
and eventually become a
nationwide organization of 10,000.

86
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:43,920
And you'll stand at its very top.

87
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:47,740
The top of 10,000? Will my salary go up too?

88
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:51,240
Of course. Twice what it is now,
three times, no, ten times.

89
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,018
No,

90
00:05:52,068 --> 00:05:57,560
now that I think about it,
only I could handle such a difficult job.

91
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,100
Yo, you'll do it?

92
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,900
Let's protect Japan's skies together.

93
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:09,580
And this is the flying
machine that matters most?

94
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:13,680
Don't worry,
I've factored in air resistance properly.

95
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:15,660
That's not the issue, is it?

96
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,980
There's no way this thing can fly!

97
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,960
What are you saying, young man?

98
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:23,000
This is based on Leonardo
da Vinci's blueprints,

99
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
which I modified and built myself.

100
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,760
I call it the Leonardo Esaki No. 1.

101
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:31,080
A collaboration between the
Italian genius of the Renaissance

102
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,400
and a modern Japanese genius.

103
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:41,500
...No test flight? So you've tested it yourself?
If you're that confident, you must have flown it personally, right?

104
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:50,980
Th-that's obviously true! Then fly it again right in front of me.
Oh no, it's siesta time already!

105
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:57,020
Siesta? In Italy, people have
the custom of napping after lunch.

106
00:06:57,020 --> 00:07:03,320
Working too hard means no brilliant ideas come to you, you see.
So, well, that's that.

107
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,940
I'm going to take my nap.

108
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,580
Hey, don't try to change the subject!

109
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:11,500
Stop your blabbering and go
on your test flight already.

110
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:13,240
Hey, you!

111
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:15,360
W-what?

112
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,178
Whoa! W-wait, wait,

113
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:20,620
What is this! I knew it, I'm the guinea pig!

114
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:23,400
Fly, Leonardo Esaki and company!

115
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,120
Yaga!

116
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,280
Nyaa!

117
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,660
Yaga!

118
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:39,820
That's why I said it couldn't possibly fly,
didn't I?

119
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:43,440
I figured your stamina would
get you through it, though.

120
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,880
So it was structurally impossible

121
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:47,740
If you knew that,
don't build it in the first place!

122
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:49,800
But rest assured,

123
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,400
this isn't the only airplane we have.

124
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:54,820
What is this?

125
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,000
This?

126
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:58,384
Based on Leonardo da Pinchi's blueprints,

127
00:07:58,434 --> 00:08:00,918
I added my own touches and built it.

128
00:08:00,968 --> 00:08:03,740
It's said to be the model
for today's helicopters.

129
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:09,383
Today there are proper helicopters, you know!
Just to be safe, I'll ask,

130
00:08:09,433 --> 00:08:11,800
you did test-fly it properly, right?

131
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:13,720
W-well, now, let me think.

132
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:14,780
Don't try to dodge the question!

133
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:16,840
Alright, time for my siesta.

134
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:19,680
You already had your siesta earlier!

135
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:22,481
You really are a man who
fusses over the smallest things.

136
00:08:22,531 --> 00:08:24,340
You'll be hated in Italy for that.

137
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:29,500
Stop your bickering and
go test-fly it already.

138
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,680
Pedal it.

139
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,780
Fly, Leonardo Esaki No. 2!

140
00:08:45,540 --> 00:09:15,020
Waaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah...
Aaaah... Aah, aah, aah, aah, aah, aah, aah!

141
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,960
If there's a car in between, we have to cross
the bridge every time just to get around, don't we!

142
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,320
Never mind that, just look at this.

143
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:24,780
W-what's this?

144
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:30,540
Surprised This one is aptly
named Leonardo Esaki No. 3!

145
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:33,780
All you've shown me so far are
human-powered flying machines.

146
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:38,000
The Air Police Unit was only just formed,
so the budget is still small.

147
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:41,700
But this one actually
looks like it might fly.

148
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:45,680
Did you base this one on Leonardo
Da Pinchi's blueprints too?

149
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:50,580
No, I copied that idea from
the Bikkuri Birdman Contest.

150
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:54,000
Then there's no need to bother calling it Leonardo,
is there?

151
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,760
Fussing over details like that will make you hated in Italy,
you know.

152
00:09:57,760 --> 00:10:00,600
I keep telling you, this is Japan!

153
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:07,820
As for this one, the test flight...

154
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:10,960
Asking was a waste of time

155
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,880
Anyway, I'll give it a try.

156
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:28,140
Speed it up! Faster!

157
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,900
It's fine! Keep pedaling just like that!

158
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:39,420
N-no, no! It's no good!

159
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:43,860
Idiot! That's Ryo-san's own responsibility!

160
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,840
Then you try it!

161
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:48,360
Oops, it's siesta time!

162
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:49,380
Don't sleep on duty!

163
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:52,260
Whoa! What?!

164
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,860
Well, screw it!

165
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,700
Yes! It flew!

166
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,400
I can't believe it actually flew.

167
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,320
You're one to talk!

168
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:10,520
Feels like I've become a bird.

169
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,580
What is that guy?

170
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,540
He must be speeding.

171
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,760
Hey, Nakagawa, this is bad!

172
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,900
He's speeding toward
the 3-chome intersection!

173
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:22,580
Yes, understood!

174
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:26,160
Here he comes!

175
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:29,900
You on the motorcycle, stop! Stop!

176
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,580
How did they figure it out?

177
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:32,180
Damn it.

178
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:36,660
Shoot.

179
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:42,220
The suspect's motorcycle is
heading for the 3-chome intersection.

180
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,040
No, wait a minute.

181
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,780
He ducked into a back road again.

182
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:48,280
He really knows his back alleys.

183
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:50,420
At this rate, he might get away.

184
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,700
In that case, I'll

185
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:56,260
Think a patrol car can catch me?

186
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:56,980
Wait! Wait!

187
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:01,200
You're under arrest!

188
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:07,200
Giving us a lot of trouble, aren't you?

189
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:10,960
Senpai.

190
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,460
We've already done it!

191
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:15,400
The Air Police Unit is a
huge success from day one!

192
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:16,700
Senpai.

193
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:17,860
At this rate,

194
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:20,140
the ATM robbery case too,

195
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:21,260
you'll catch them too, won't you?

196
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,660
Leave it to me!

197
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:25,780
But the plane you came in on...

198
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:28,580
It's already way over there!

199
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,660
No need to be surprised.

200
00:12:30,660 --> 00:12:37,520
That plane is a perfect copy of the one that set an
immeasurable record at the Bikkuri Torinin Contest!

201
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:39,400
It'll fly to the ends of the earth!

202
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:41,620
But over there is the ocean!

203
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,720
Maybe we should just give up.

204
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:48,260
It's gone! That one decent plane we had...

205
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,620
Now that we've caught the criminal,

206
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:07,220
it looks like the time has come to show
the true power of the Air Police Unit.

207
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,900
Then what was all that before?

208
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,760
Now, take a look at this.

209
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:18,020
It's the Leonardo Esaki No. 5.

210
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:19,800
That's not bad at all.

211
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:25,680
Wait, in order,
shouldn't the next one be No. 4?

212
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:28,340
No. 4 performed poorly, so I skipped it.

213
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:31,220
You're awfully Japanese when
it comes to things like that.

214
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:35,440
It has an engine after all.
And you said there was no budget.

215
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:39,680
It'd be a waste not to use that animal-like stamina of yours,
wouldn't it?

216
00:13:39,940 --> 00:13:43,162
Besides, we can't keep polluting
the earth's atmosphere any further,

217
00:13:43,212 --> 00:13:46,200
so I'm aiming for an eco-friendly airplane.

218
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:50,660
That's why I made this flying
machine run on electricity too.

219
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:52,760
It has one drawback.

220
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:53,620
Drawback?

221
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:58,860
It takes an incredibly long time to charge.

222
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:00,640
About five hours, give or take.

223
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,520
Why didn't you charge it beforehand?

224
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:06,680
Well then, I'll take a siesta
until the charging is complete.

225
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,580
Ouch, good night.

226
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:11,020
What a man who sleeps a lot.

227
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:20,380
It's already evening, so get up already.

228
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:24,165
Wow, what a refreshing awakening.

229
00:14:24,215 --> 00:14:27,360
How beautiful, what a beautiful sunrise.

230
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:28,980
It's a sunset.

231
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:32,340
Fuss over such small things
in Italy and you'll be hated.

232
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,570
I keep telling you, this is Japan.

233
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:37,280
The charging should be
almost finished by now, right?

234
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,520
Let's see. Yeah, looks good.

235
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:42,940
Well then,
let's go for a test run right away.

236
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,500
Does this flying machine have two seats?

237
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:52,080
When I added two engines,
I got carried away and put in two seats too.

238
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:53,460
I see.

239
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:55,800
W-what? Don't tell me...

240
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:59,800
There are two seats, so let's ride together.

241
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:02,700
N-no, I'll have to pass.

242
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:05,180
I have to collect data from outside.

243
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:07,840
You'd get more accurate data if you rode it.

244
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:10,700
I-it's time, I have to sleep.

245
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,700
You slept plenty just now!

246
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:17,140
Or don't you have confidence
in the flying machine you built?

247
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,500
Don't joke around like that.

248
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,880
The flying machine I built is perfect.

249
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:22,820
Then get on it.

250
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:28,320
Don't underestimate me, Gorilla-kun.

251
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:31,340
You really are the type who
judges by appearances first.

252
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:33,100
Fine, then here I go.

253
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,660
Engine start!

254
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:42,540
Takeoff!

255
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:46,160
Whoa, it's running!

256
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:48,760
Well, of course,
it's gliding along the ground.

257
00:15:52,180 --> 00:15:53,740
Whoa, we're floating! We're floating!

258
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:55,280
You're so annoying, always nitpicking.

259
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:57,800
Never mind that.
Are we really leaving the wheels behind?

260
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,360
They add too much weight,
so I detached them.

261
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,160
What about when we land?

262
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:07,180
Fret over such petty details
and you'll be hated in Italy.

263
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:08,300
This is Japan.

264
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,660
Much easier than pedaling by hand

265
00:16:15,660 --> 00:16:17,380
Minus, minus.

266
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:20,140
Don't tell me you're afraid of heights?

267
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:23,080
Don't make jokes like that.

268
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,780
Idiot, that's dangerous!

269
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:28,140
I have nothing to fear.

270
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:40,820
So, how about it?

271
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:44,540
Now you know I'm not
afraid of heights, right?

272
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:46,220
You were passed out, though.

273
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:48,360
What's that noise?

274
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:51,320
We're out of fuel!
The electricity's run out!

275
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:55,320
Wait, it's not even been five
minutes since we took off!

276
00:16:55,820 --> 00:17:00,140
This plane can only fly for five
minutes after five hours of a full charge!

277
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:02,820
That's completely useless, then!

278
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:09,640
Don't worry, Gorilla-kun.
For situations like this,

279
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:12,920
W-what is it?

280
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:16,540
Pedal it! That'll recharge it.

281
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:17,120
What?

282
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:25,600
Hurry up and pedal!

283
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:26,100
Did it work?

284
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:36,400
Yes, it worked!

285
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:39,060
This is no different from
a human-powered plane!

286
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,040
Setup complete.

287
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,200
Understood.

288
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,880
A blimp at this hour of the night?

289
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:08,880
N-no way, that's...

290
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:23,080
Looks like today's is pretty well stocked.

291
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:27,040
Once you escape into the sky, Japanese
police can't lay a finger on you, right?

292
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,220
Piece of cake.

293
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:29,080
Stop!

294
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:32,060
Did you just hear something?

295
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:33,940
No way, we're up in the sky!

296
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:35,320
Get back here!

297
00:18:37,060 --> 00:18:38,760
I'm with the Aerial Police Unit.

298
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:42,140
You're under arrest for
caught-in-the-act ATM robbery!

299
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:45,440
I never thought there'd
be an air police in Japan.

300
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:46,480
Let's get out of here!

301
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:52,800
Like I'd let you!

302
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:58,280
Hey, go faster! He's catching up!

303
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:00,560
This ATM is way too heavy!

304
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:04,440
Give up!
You can't escape carrying that thing!

305
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,340
Damn you, take this!

306
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:15,160
Come on, give up already!

307
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:17,140
What a persistent guy!

308
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,660
If it comes to this...

309
00:19:54,020 --> 00:19:56,920
Hey, miss, care to join me for a siesta?

310
00:19:58,960 --> 00:19:59,900
Wait up!

311
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,060
Damn it,
I can't shake him off no matter what!

312
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,540
This is it, this signal's the one!

313
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,360
He's not coming!

314
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:17,860
There's a hole!

315
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,940
That's why fabric wings are such a pain!

316
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:24,780
Don't worry, I've got spare fabric
ready for just this sort of thing.

317
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:29,360
Right, then I'll go sew it on.
You take the controls while I'm gone.

318
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:31,240
Me?

319
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:35,340
Who else is there?
Or are you going to sew it up yourself?

320
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:41,700
I'll let you have that glamorous role.
I'll stick to working behind the scenes.

321
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:46,700
All you have to do is hold the control stick and keep pedaling,
so don't go messing with anything else.

322
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:51,280
It's a shame I can't show off my
brilliant piloting skills, though.

323
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:53,080
In that case,
I guess there's no help for it.

324
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,200
This is really hard to work with.

325
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,680
What are you doing, all of a sudden?

326
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:06,220
It's just a little performance test.

327
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:09,080
Damn, the fabric fell off.

328
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:11,120
Don't you have any spares?

329
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:12,500
What?

330
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:44,020
That was close!

331
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:48,580
Right in the middle of aerobatics,
and it's already siesta time.

332
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:50,520
You only passed out, you know.

333
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:56,100
Think you've gotten away, do you?
Relaxing already?

334
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:59,380
Alright, I'll take advantage of
this opening and hit them from above!

335
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:06,080
Okay, let's go!

336
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:07,320
That pervert.

337
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:07,900
What?

338
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:10,480
Because the moon is so blue.

339
00:22:13,220 --> 00:22:15,220
A pervert man was flying.

340
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,300
Dead from the moon, Moonlight, is it?

341
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:19,900
Venus too, is it?

342
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:22,040
I'm back, Kenzan.

343
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,320
Why are you guys showing up?

344
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,960
And don't go standing on top of the plane!

345
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:28,980
That's way too unnatural!

346
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:31,960
I don't seem to be feeling well tonight.

347
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:33,420
I'm seeing strange hallucinations.

348
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:34,580
It's reality.

349
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:37,040
Damn it!

350
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:38,640
An escape device, is it?

351
00:22:40,260 --> 00:22:41,440
Sorry, Gorilla-kun.

352
00:22:42,460 --> 00:22:43,660
You irresponsible...

353
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,460
That pervert!

354
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:49,700
You're under arrest for theft in the act!

355
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:51,380
W-wait, it's me!

356
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:52,740
Don't you remember?

357
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:55,940
A violent pervert flying through
the sky with his bits hanging out.

358
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:57,440
I don't know him.

359
00:22:57,440 --> 00:23:00,000
I don't want to hear that from you people!

360
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:00,460
Yeah.

361
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:02,000
Next, let me take over.

362
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:02,880
To you guys...

363
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:05,280
Let's talk it out.

364
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:07,260
Aaaaah!

365
00:23:10,340 --> 00:23:16,240
It's too bad you couldn't steal the cash dispenser,
but you got away nicely

366
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:17,720
Aaaaah!

367
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,620
Culprit arrested! Mission complete!

368
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:25,880
Wait! I'm the one who's been robbing!

369
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:31,720
So what's going to happen to
the air police squad in the end?

370
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:33,500
It's been scrapped.

371
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:45,620
Gota got arrested, right? But we don't need two groups of flying weirdos,
so now we're creating an underground police squad.

372
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:54,240
Now then, Gorilla-kun, you two will help build up the underground police squad.
The peace of the underground is in our hands.

373
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:59,820
Shut up! What kind of crime could
possibly happen in a place like this?

374
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:20,180
Even at midnight, the calls keep coming in.

375
00:24:20,180 --> 00:24:27,400
With you, waking up feels good.

376
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:31,820
Even boring talk

377
00:24:31,820 --> 00:24:43,220
Heating up my whole body.
But, friend, I want to see you.

378
00:24:43,220 --> 00:24:52,500
I surely want to be loved, just a little,
enough to make everyone hate it.

379
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:27,760
I'm ashamed to say that since I was commissioned as a police officer,
I have never arrested a criminal.

380
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:33,160
But at long last, the moment has come
when I finally put handcuffs on someone with my own hands.

381
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:37,880
Next time: Kanrei Terai's first experience.
Please look forward to it.

